  "goodToKnow": "Die Zeitumstellung is the clock change: on the last Sunday in March, clocks go forward to Sommerzeit, and on the last Sunday in October back to Winterzeit (officially Normalzeit). West Germany reintroduced summer time in 1980. In 2019 the European Parliament voted to end the clock changes, but member states have not agreed, so it continues. A memory aid: im Frühling stellt man die Gartenmöbel vor das Haus, im Herbst zurück. Plural: die Zeitumstellungen."
